### Architectural Audit & Fix Explanation

#### 1. Vulnerability Analysis & Cyber-Physical Friction
The adversarial dialectic identified a latent statutory antinomy between two foundational structural mandates:
1. **The Absolute Continuity Mandate (Art. 1.3.1, Art. 4.4.4):** Tier 1 metabolic lifelines (potable water, atmospheric support, baseline thermal regulation) must flow continuously; precautionary administrative suspension or artificial throttling is strictly illegal.
2. **The Anti-Technocracy Invariant (Art. 7.1.1):** Autonomous algorithmic calculation engines are categorically prohibited from determining, rationing, curtailing, or adjudicating human resource entitlements.

Under edge-case physical failure regimes (e.g., severe cavitation in high-pressure reverse osmosis pumps, transducer calibration drift, thermal runaway in membrane manifolds), deterministic Programmable Logic Controllers (PLCs) must execute emergency trips, throttling, or line cutoffs to prevent catastrophic, irreversible equipment destruction. Under an unpatched, hyper-literal reading of Articles 4.4.4 and 7.1.1:
- An automated PLC trip could be legally construed as an unconstitutional algorithmic rationing event or an administrative curtailment of baseline rights.
- Conversely, forbidding deterministic trip routines forces equipment to operate into irreversible mechanical destruction, paradoxically violating Chapter I by physically terminating the life-support substrate.

#### 2. Architectural Remedy & Mechanics
The amendment formally resolves this boundary friction without compromising Chapter I invariants by introducing the following structural codifications:
- **Delineation of Sovereign Rationing vs. Deterministic Asset Protection (Art. 7.1.1 & Art. 7.1.3):** Establishes an explicit boundary between *political-economic rationing* (allocating scarce resources among persons, which remains strictly sovereign and human-adjudicated) and *deterministic thermodynamic interlocks* (closed-loop physical asset protection preventing mechanical self-destruction).
- **Multi-Transducer Plausibility Voting (Art. 6.3.3 & Art. 7.1.3):** Mandates triple-modular redundancy (2-of-3 physical plausibility voting across independent galvanic/piezoelectric/optical channels) before any protective throttling or trip sequence can trigger, eliminating single-sensor spoofing or transducer drift exploits.
- **Mandatory Deterministic Failover to Passive Strategic Reserves (Art. 4.4.4 & Art. 1.3.1):** Codifies that any protective equipment cutoff must *simultaneously and automatically trigger passive, non-electric, gravity-fed hydraulic draw from the strategic reserve envelope (Art. 3.5.2 / 6.5.2)*, ensuring zero interruption in the physical delivery of baseline metabolic lifelines to the human populace.

